+# Round 13 research report
+
+## Current checkpoint
+
+PROVED scope and conventions: this report follows `tdense13_brief.md`. Computations will run only through `DIRICHLET_IP=34.148.157.169 src/dirun.sh -c 4`; no subagents, commits, LaTeX, or edits to top-level research Markdown files. Existing unrelated workspace changes are preserved. The report and `tdense13_scratch/` hold this round's work.
+
+PROVED target: for every odd prime q admitting a symmetric set B excluding 0 with |B|=(q−1)/2, write λ(γ)=sum over c in B of exp(2πiγc/q), K=−min over γ≠0 of λ(γ), and Λ=max over γ≠0 of λ(γ). This convention is feasible only for q≡1 mod 4; q≡3 mod 4 requires toggling 0 or changing cardinality by one. Seek a proved quantitative uniformity statement QU(β), a conditional statement surviving the specified fakes, or an explicit partial-convolution relaxation barrier. No exponent improvement is claimed at this checkpoint.
+
+PROVED quoted project state: P61–P64, NOTEBOOK continuations 15–17, E41, E82, and the round-12 report are being audited as inputs. P63's unconditional dense endpoint is C<2000/259. P61's second-order reach and R12-S are quoted results, not discoveries of this round.
+
+HEURISTIC research frontier:
+
+| Known | Exact gap | Candidate mechanism | Discriminating test |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Exact binary convolution at every nonzero frequency | Quantitative gain from several frequencies | Positive mass must meet threshold negatives at many translates | Derive a weighted mixed-pair deficit identity and test saturation |
+| PK is stronger than uniformity | Whether genuine half-sets refute PK | Symmetric random rounding of a positive Fourier profile | Prove concentration and certify finite cyclic spectra |
+| R12-S matches selected scalar constraints | Higher additive-count integrality and positivity | Integral spectra with prescribed first two moments | Exact power-sum divisibility and all-order argument |
+| Weighted P61 escapes attain the second-order reach | Binary realization | Near-interval, Paley-scale, and spectral-error-diffusion rounding | VM FFT/refinement, with Arb point values for every dip |
+
+PROVED input audit completed: read CLAUDE.md, P61–P64, NOTEBOOK continuations 15–17, E41, E82's profile definition, and the round-12 report. The round brief overrides CLAUDE.md's generic commit and top-level-record instructions. No applicable AGENTS.md was found in the workspace or its ancestors. VM dependency check: Python 3.12.3, NumPy 2.5.4, SciPy 1.18.1, Gurobi 13.0.3, python-flint 0.9.0.
+
+NUMERICAL work in progress: `cyclic_probe.py` is running on the prescribed VM. It tests cosine-profile rounding and Gurobi trade-offs for q=17,37,61,89,101,109. For q≤89 the input K-minima are quoted E41 double-precision enumeration results; the new q=101,109 K-min searches are time-limited and will be labelled by their actual bounds/status. Arb certifies every spectrum of a reported trade-off incumbent. Gurobi optimality with floating cosine coefficients is not an exact algebraic optimality certificate.
+
+## PK is false: a genuine binary family
+
+PROVED R13-PK. Fix any ε with 0<ε<1/2. For every sufficiently large prime q≡1 mod 4 there exists B=−B⊂Z_q, 0∉B, |B|=(q−1)/2, with
+
+    λ(1)=εq/2+O(√(q log q)),
+    λ(γ)≥−O(√(q log q)) for every γ≠0.
+
+The constants may depend on ε. Consequently, for every fixed η>0 and C>0, the assertion Λ≤C K^(2−η) fails for some such B. This is an unconditional refutation of PK, rather than a relaxation example.
+
+PROVED proof. For a=1,…,(q−1)/2 choose independent bits Y_a with means p_a=1/2+ε cos(2πa/q), and include both ±a when Y_a=1. Extend the mean profile to c=0 by the same formula. Discrete orthogonality gives, for γ≠0, expected λ(γ)=εq/2−(1/2+ε) at γ=±1 and −(1/2+ε) at every other γ. The expected number of selected pairs is (q−1)/4−ε/2.
+
+For completeness, the bounded-variable exponential estimate used here follows by convexity of exp on each variable's range: a centred variable of range length d has exponential moment at most exp(t²d²/8). Multiply these estimates for independent variables, then optimize t. Each Fourier sum has range lengths at most 2 per pair, so the probability of an error exceeding u is at most 2 exp(−u²/(q−1)). The pair count has the same or better estimate. A union bound, with u=3√(q log q), supplies one outcome where every nonzero Fourier sum and the count have that error bound. Flip at most u+1 pairs to obtain exactly (q−1)/4 pairs; this changes every λ by at most 2u+2. Thus λ(1)=εq/2+O(√(q log q)) and K=O(√(q log q)), as claimed. Since K>0 (the nonzero Fourier trace is negative), Λ/K^(2−η) tends to infinity for 0<η≤2; η>2 is immediate from the same bounds and K≥1/2. Infinitely many primes q≡1 mod 4 follow from the elementary prime-divisor argument for (2p₁⋯p_r)²+1.
+
+PROVED compatibility with QU: these examples cannot falsify a small-δ assertion. The quoted exact second-order peak inequality Λ²≤Λ+2K(K−1/2)(q−1), together with λ(1)∼εq/2, forces K≥(ε/(2√2)+o(1))√q. Their normalized negative threshold stays bounded away from zero.
+
+PROVED bookkeeping correction/check. If QU(β) holds, combine Λ≥((q+1)/4−K²)/(K−1/2) with Λ≤Cq(K/√q)^β in the regime K≤δ₀√q, shrinking δ₀<1/4 if necessary. This yields K^(β+1)≥c q^(β/2) and hence K≥c' q^(β/(2β+2))=c' q^(1/2−1/(2(β+1))). Outside that regime the square-root lower bound already dominates. Thus β=1 gives 1/4 and β=2 gives 1/3. The notation β=∞ is a limiting aspiration, not a literal finite-constant theorem.
+
+## Main result: an exact partial-convolution barrier
+
+PROVED R13-C (paper proof; independent finite checks pending). Let J(q) be any positive-integer function with J(q)=o(q^(1/3)). For every sufficiently large odd prime q there is a real even array λ on Z_q satisfying all the following:
+
+- λ(0)=(q−1)/2, sum λ=0, and sum λ²=q(q−1)/2, exactly;
+- −min over γ≠0 of λ(γ)=q^(1/3)/2;
+- max over γ≠0 of λ(γ)=λ(1)=2q^(2/3)−q^(1/3)/2;
+- sum over β≠0,γ of λ(β)λ(γ−β)=λ(γ), exactly, for every γ in ±{1,…,J(q)}.
+
+PROVED consequence: this explicit relaxation, including the convolution identity along an increasing initial segment of the peak orbit, is consistent with exponent 1/3. In this relaxation δ=K/√q=(1/2)q^(−1/6) and Λ∼2q^(2/3), so QU(β) fails for every β>2. This is the requested barrier deliverable. The arrays need not be binary Fourier transforms. The assertion does not preserve the identity outside the specified segment, all additive-count integrality conditions, or every inequality that could be deduced using the missing equations.
+
+PROVED construction and full proof. Write u=q^(1/3), H=4u², ℓ=ceil(u), and C=q u(u−2). We construct a nonnegative even h and then set z=h−u. Impose h(0)=u−1, h(±1)=H, and require
+
+    sum h=q(u−1),     sum h²=q²+q u(u−2).
+
+These imply sum z=−q, sum z²=q², z(0)=−1. Also z*z(γ)=h*h(γ)−C, where convolution is the unnormalized cyclic sum. Here h is even, so h*h(γ) equals its autocorrelation at displacement γ.
+
+The already placed three sites contribute R₁=2(u−1)H at displacement 1, R₂=H² at displacement 2, and R_d=0 at every d≥3. Set R₂=0 if J=1 is irrelevant; for d=1,…,J the intended residual is C−R_d>0 for all sufficiently large q. For each d choose ℓ disjoint positive two-site clusters {t,t+d} and their reflected clusters {−t,−t−d}. Put the same amplitude
+
+    a_d=sqrt((C−R_d)/(2ℓ))
+
+on their four sites. Require that different clusters, the three original sites, and the eventual repair sites are at cyclic distances greater than J from one another. Within one pair, the two reflected edges contribute exactly 2a_d² to the autocorrelation at d; there are no other contributions at displacements 1,…,J. Thus h*h(d)=R_d+2ℓ a_d²=C for every d in the required segment.
+
+The cluster sites use mass 4ℓ sum a_d=O(Jq) and energy 4ℓ sum a_d²=O(Jq^(5/3)). The original sites use mass O(q^(2/3)) and energy O(q^(4/3)). Since J=o(q^(1/3)), the remaining mass T and energy E obey
+
+    T∼q^(4/3),     E∼q²,     T²/E∼q^(2/3).
+
+They are positive. Choose m=4 ceil(3T²/(8E)), μ=T/m, and v=E/m−μ². For sufficiently large q,
+
+    (3/2)T²/E≤m≤2T²/E,
+    0≤v≤μ²,     μ+sqrt(v)≤2μ≤(4/3)E/T<4q^(2/3)=H.
+
+Put μ+sqrt(v) on m/2 repair sites and μ−sqrt(v) on m/2 repair sites, each group itself a union of reflected pairs. They supply mass T and energy E exactly and stay nonnegative. The cluster amplitudes also satisfy a_d∼q^(2/3)/sqrt(2)<H, uniformly in d. Consequently H is the maximum h and occurs at ±1.
+
+PROVED spacing and capacity detail. Place the positive clusters one after another, using a block of length 3J+3 per cluster, starting beyond 4J+10. A pair at {t,t+d} leaves a gap greater than J before the next cluster. Then place the positive repair sites with spacing 2J+2 and reflect all these sites across 0. The used half-line length is
+
+    O(J²ℓ+Jm)=O(J²q^(1/3)+Jq^(2/3))=o(q).
+
+Thus all positive sites lie below q/2−2J for sufficiently large q. This also separates every reflected pair of different clusters across the midpoint; the initial gap separates them across 0. The only near-0 sites are the three explicitly accounted for. Hence there are no wraparound correlations at the specified displacements. The total support is o(q), so some offzero sites have h=0 and min z=−u exactly.
+
+Finally define λ(0)=(q−1)/2 and λ(γ)=z(γ)/2 for γ≠0. Equivalently z=2λ−qδ₀. The trace and energy above give the asserted trace and Parseval identities for λ. At every required nonzero γ, z*z(γ)=0 is equivalent to λ*λ(γ)=qλ(γ). Removing the β=0,γ contributions, whose sum is (q−1)λ(γ), proves exactly the asserted off-zero equation. Evenness supplies the negative γ equations. This completes the proof.
+
+PROVED adversarial scope check. The construction has a genuine peak at 1 and preserves the γ=2 equation containing its square; it does not evade that equation by moving the peak outside the tested orbit. Every fixed number of equations is covered, and J can grow as any o(q^(1/3)) function. It also obeys the scalar second-order peak bound and the R12 scalar cubic peak bound for sufficiently large q. The evenly spaced repair sites may produce large correlations at untested displacements, so no claim that this is an approximate solution of all q equations is made.
+
+PROVED exact mixed-pair deficit identity (a diagnostic, not an exponent improvement). Extend P,N by zero at frequency 0 and write S=sum P, D_γ=sum over β of P(β)[K−N(γ−β)]. Every term in D_γ is nonnegative. At every γ where binary convolution holds,
+
+    (P*P)(γ)+(N*N)(γ)+2D_γ=λ(γ)+2KS.
+
+This follows by expanding λ=P−N on nonzero indices and substituting P*N=KS−D_γ. Thus the candidate pairing incompatibility must use the arrangement of deficits at additional frequencies. R13-C proves that the first o(q^(1/3)) peak-orbit equations alone cannot establish β>2 in the stated relaxation.
+
+HEURISTIC strategic review after the PK obstruction and partial-convolution construction: discontinue universal PK and a fixed-J incompatibility argument. Continue the full-frequency incidence/additive-energy approach and additive-count arithmetic; both use information explicitly absent from R13-C. The construction side remains independent and is now running. No unconditional exponent improvement or new dense endpoint is claimed.
diff --git a/.research/agents/tdense13_scratch/barrier_check.py b/.research/agents/tdense13_scratch/barrier_check.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..140a5b80e633ebd51f85e20b8f3224f710c5a171
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.research/agents/tdense13_scratch/barrier_check.py
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+"""Exact support geometry plus 180-bit Arb checks of the partial-convolution construction."""
+from pathlib import Path
+from fractions import Fraction as Q
+import json, math
+from flint import arb,ctx
+import sympy as sp
+ctx.prec=180
+ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
+
+def barrier(q,J):
+    # q is an integer cube in these rational checks. The paper proof covers every sufficiently large odd prime.
+    u=round(q**(1/3));assert u**3==q
+    H=4*u*u;C=q*u*(u-2);ell=u
+    residual=[None]+[Q(C-2*(u-1)*H if d==1 else C-H*H if d==2 else C) for d in range(1,J+1)]
+    assert all(v>0 for v in residual[1:])
+    special={0:(0,1),1:(1,1),q-1:(1,1)}
+    # Symbolic labels: 0=h0, 1=H, 1+d=dedicated-pair amplitude, J+2/J+3=repair levels.
+    levels=[arb(u-1),arb(H)]+[(arb(v.numerator)/v.denominator/(2*ell)).sqrt() for v in residual[1:]]
+    t=4*J+10
+    for d in range(1,J+1):
+        for _ in range(ell):
+            for a in (t,t+d,q-t,q-t-d):
+                assert a not in special;special[a]=(d+1,1)
+            t+=3*J+3
+    T=arb(q*(u-1))-levels[0]-2*levels[1]
+    E=arb(q*q+q*u*(u-2))-levels[0]**2-2*levels[1]**2
+    for d in range(1,J+1):T-=4*ell*levels[d+1];E-=2*residual[d]
+    assert T.lower()>0 and E.lower()>0
+    ratio=T*T/E;m=4*math.ceil(float((3*ratio/8).mid()))
+    assert (arb(m)-ratio).lower()>0 and (2*ratio-m).lower()>0
+    mean=T/m;var=E/m-mean*mean
+    assert var.lower()>0 and (mean*mean-var).lower()>0
+    levels += [mean+var.sqrt(),mean-var.sqrt()]
+    assert (levels[1]-levels[-2]).lower()>0
+    for idx in range(m//2):
+        t+=2*J+2
+        label=J+2 if idx<m//4 else J+3
+        for a in (t,q-t):assert a not in special;special[a]=(label,1)
+    assert t+3*J<q//2
+    correlations=[]
+    for d in range(1,J+1):
+        counts={}
+        for a,(la,_) in special.items():
+            b=(a+d)%q
+            if b in special:
+                lb=special[b][0];key=tuple(sorted((la,lb)))
+                counts[key]=counts.get(key,0)+1
+        expected={(d+1,d+1):2*ell}
+        if d==1:expected[(0,1)]=2
+        if d==2:expected[(1,1)]=1
+        assert counts==expected,(d,counts,expected)
+        value=sum((mult*levels[a]*levels[b] for (a,b),mult in counts.items()),arb(0))
+        assert (value-C).contains(0)
+        correlations.append(dict(gamma=d,exact_monomial_counts={str(k):v for k,v in counts.items()},
+                                 residual_ball=str(value-C)))
+    mass=levels[0]+2*levels[1]+sum((4*ell*levels[d+1] for d in range(1,J+1)),arb(0))+m*mean
+    energy=levels[0]**2+2*levels[1]**2+sum((4*ell*levels[d+1]**2 for d in range(1,J+1)),arb(0))+m*(mean*mean+var)
+    assert (mass-q*(u-1)).contains(0)
+    assert (energy-(q*q+q*u*(u-2))).contains(0)
+    return dict(q=q,prime=False,J=J,u=u,repair_sites=m,support_sites=len(special),last_positive=t,
+                K_sign=u,Lambda_sign=H-u,mass_residual=str(mass-q*(u-1)),
+                energy_residual=str(energy-(q*q+q*u*(u-2))),correlations=correlations,
+                status='Exact support-count check and Arb arithmetic; infinite-prime claim proved in report')
+
+def fake_cubic():
+    # Work in Q[u]/(u^3-q); m is the even support count of R12-S.
+    u,q,m=sp.symbols('u q m')
+    T=(q-1)*(u-1)
+    E=q*q+q*u*(u-2)-(u-1)**2
+    H=T/m;v=E/m-H*H
+    moment=sp.expand(m*((H-u)**3+3*(H-u)*v)+(q-1-m)*(-u)**3)
+    rem=sp.rem(moment,u**3-q,u)
+    return dict(sign_third_moment=str(sp.factor(rem)),coefficients={str(k):str(sp.factor(rem.coeff(u,k))) for k in range(3)},
+                note='Nonzero u or u^2 coefficient implies irrationality for prime q.')
+
+if __name__=='__main__':
+    result=dict(barrier=[barrier(u**3,J) for u,J in ((200,3),(400,5),(800,8))],fake_cubic=fake_cubic())
+    (ROOT/'barrier_checks.json').write_text(json.dumps(result,indent=2))
+    print(json.dumps(result,indent=2),flush=True)
diff --git a/.research/agents/tdense13_scratch/binary_probe.py b/.research/agents/tdense13_scratch/binary_probe.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..6893baee74ec6aec3cb49acf6c24d833fd651704
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.research/agents/tdense13_scratch/binary_probe.py
@@ -0,0 +1,117 @@
+"""Profile-preserving binary laws. FFT estimates, refined dips, Arb point certificates."""
+from pathlib import Path
+import ctypes,json,math,subprocess,sys,gc,platform
+import numpy as np
+from scipy.optimize import minimize_scalar
+from sympy import nextprime
+import gurobipy as gp
+from gurobipy import GRB
+from flint import arb,ctx
+ctx.prec=180
+ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
+
+def profile(X):
+    rows=[json.loads(l) for l in open('examples/e82/e82.jsonl')]
+    row=max((r for r in rows if r['N']==320),key=lambda r:r['D'])
+    g=np.array(row['g']);w0=np.r_[np.correlate(g,g,'full')[319:]/(g@g),0]
+    w=np.interp(np.arange(1,X+1)/X,np.arange(321)/320,w0)
+    return (1-np.sqrt(np.maximum(0,1-w*w)))/2,w
+
+def prime1(x):
+    q=int(nextprime(max(4,int(x)-1)))
+    while q%4!=1:q=int(nextprime(q))
+    return q
+
+def counted(p,scores,B=256):
+    out=np.zeros(len(p),dtype=np.uint8);carry=0.
+    for lo in range(0,len(p),B):
+        hi=min(lo+B,len(p));target=float(p[lo:hi].sum())+carry
+        cnt=int(round(target));carry=target-cnt
+        take=np.argsort(-scores[lo:hi],kind='stable')[:cnt]+lo;out[take]=1
+    return out
+
+def minimum(bits):
+    X=len(bits);A=np.flatnonzero(bits).astype(np.int64)+1
+    L=1<<(16*(X+1)-1).bit_length();coef=np.zeros(X+1);coef[1:]=bits
+    vals=np.fft.rfft(coef,n=L).real
+    js=np.argpartition(vals,min(16,len(vals)-1))[:16]
+    j=int(vals.argmin());best=float(vals[j]);phase=j/L
+    del vals;gc.collect()
+    def f(t):return float(np.cos(2*np.pi*A*t).sum())
+    for jj in js:
+        sol=minimize_scalar(f,bounds=(max(0,(jj-1)/L),min(.5,(jj+1)/L)),method='bounded',
+                            options={'xatol':1e-16,'maxiter':40})
+        if sol.fun<best:best=float(sol.fun);phase=float(sol.x)
+    # Evaluate an exact rational phase, so the point is unambiguous and independently reproducible.
+    den=1<<60;num=int(round(phase*den));v=arb(0)
+    for a in A:v+=(2*arb.pi()*int((int(a)*num)%den)/den).cos()
+    assert v.upper()<0
+    return dict(X=X,n=len(A),actual_max=int(A[-1]),M_estimate=-best,R_estimate=-best/math.sqrt(len(A)),
+                M_over_sqrtX=-best/math.sqrt(X),phase_num=num,phase_den=den,FFT_length=L,
+                point_ball=str(v),M_point_interval=[float(np.nextafter(-float(v.upper()),-np.inf)),
+                                                    float(np.nextafter(-float(v.lower()),np.inf))],
+                certificate_status='Arb point dip; global minimum NUMERICAL',arb_bits=ctx.prec),A
+
+def save(family,bits,extra):
+    row,A=minimum(bits);row.update(family=family,**extra)
+    np.savez_compressed(ROOT/(family+'_X'+str(len(bits))+'.npz'),A=A)
+    with open(ROOT/'binary_results.jsonl','a') as fh:fh.write(json.dumps(row)+'\n')
+    print(json.dumps(row),flush=True)
+    if row['R_estimate']<.56:
+        raise RuntimeError('Promising R<0.56: require all-x Arb certification before continuing.')
+    return row
+
+def diffusion(p,w,X):
+    # Initial adverse frequencies are the worst residual dips of a deterministic counted random seed.
+    rng=np.random.default_rng(1913+X);b=counted(p,rng.random(X))
+    L=1<<(4*(X+1)-1).bit_length();c=np.zeros(X+1);c[1:]=b-p
+    vals=np.fft.rfft(c,n=L).real;idx=np.argpartition(vals,48)[:48]
+    angles=np.r_[2*np.pi*idx/L,2*np.pi*rng.random(16)].astype(np.float64)
+    so=ROOT/'diffuse.so'
+    if not so.exists():subprocess.run(['cc','-O3','-shared','-fPIC',str(ROOT/'diffuse.c'),'-o',str(so),'-lm'],check=True)
+    lib=ctypes.CDLL(str(so));fn=lib.diffuse
+    ptr=ctypes.POINTER(ctypes.c_double)
+    fn.argtypes=[ctypes.c_int,ctypes.c_int,ctypes.c_int,ptr,ptr,ptr,ctypes.POINTER(ctypes.c_ubyte)]
+    out=np.zeros(X,dtype=np.uint8)
+    fn(X,len(angles),256,p.ctypes.data_as(ptr),w.ctypes.data_as(ptr),angles.ctypes.data_as(ptr),
+       out.ctypes.data_as(ctypes.POINTER(ctypes.c_ubyte)))
+    return out
+
+def milp(X):
+    p,w=profile(X);B=16;target=counted(p,np.cos(np.arange(X)));cuts=np.arange(16*X+1)/(32*X)
+    b0=target
+    for it in range(3):
+        model=gp.Model();model.Params.OutputFlag=0;model.Params.Threads=4;model.Params.TimeLimit=10
+        model.Params.Seed=1913
+        b=model.addMVar(X,vtype=GRB.BINARY);M=model.addVar(lb=0)
+        b.Start=b0
+        for lo in range(0,X,B):model.addConstr(b[lo:lo+B].sum()==int(target[lo:lo+B].sum()))
+        for cs in np.array_split(cuts,16):
+            C=np.cos(2*np.pi*np.outer(cs,np.arange(1,X+1)))
+            model.addConstr(C@b+M>=0)
+        model.setObjective(M);model.optimize()
+        if not model.SolCount:break
+        b0=(b.X>.5).astype(np.uint8)
+        row,A=minimum(b0);cuts=np.r_[cuts,row['phase_num']/row['phase_den']]
+    return save('gurobi_round',b0,dict(block=B,solver=gp.gurobi.version(),solver_status=int(model.Status),
+                    solver_bound=float(model.ObjBound),grid_objective=float(model.ObjVal),iterations=3))
+
+def main():
+    (ROOT/'binary_results.jsonl').write_text('')
+    for X in (4096,65536,1048576):
+        p,w=profile(X);k=np.arange(1,X+1)
+        for theta in (.5,2/3,1.):
+            q=prime1(X**theta);chi=np.zeros(q);r=np.arange(1,(q+1)//2,dtype=np.int64)
+            chi[(r*r)%q]=1
+            rng=np.random.default_rng(191300+q);tie=rng.random((q+1)//2)
+            scores=chi[k%q]+tie[np.minimum(k%q,(-k)%q)]*.1
+            save('paley_'+str(theta),counted(p,scores),dict(q=q,theta=theta,block=256,seed=191300+q))
+        for theta in (.5,1.):
+            q=prime1(X**theta)
+            # Near-interval local order, dilated by 3; exact block counts enforce the E82 profile.
+            scores=-np.minimum((3*k)%q,(-3*k)%q).astype(float)
+            save('nearinterval_'+str(theta),counted(p,scores),dict(q=q,theta=theta,dilation=3,block=256))
+        save('spectral_diffusion',diffusion(p,w,X),dict(modes=64,block=256,seed=1913+X))
+    for X in (128,256):milp(X)
+
+if __name__=='__main__':main()
diff --git a/.research/agents/tdense13_scratch/cyclic_probe.py b/.research/agents/tdense13_scratch/cyclic_probe.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..77f787dd2ead3ee8443f7f3a81ee448bb8232c3a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.research/agents/tdense13_scratch/cyclic_probe.py
@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+"""Round 13 cyclic trade-offs and profile rounding. Run only via dirun -c 4."""
+from pathlib import Path
+import json, math, re, platform, time
+import numpy as np
+import gurobipy as gp
+from gurobipy import GRB
+from flint import arb, ctx
+ctx.prec=180
+ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
+
+def balls(q, pairs):
+    values=[]
+    for g in range(1,(q+1)//2):
+        v=arb(0)
+        for a in pairs:v+=2*(2*arb.pi()*((g*a)%q)/q).cos()
+        values.append(v)
+    lo=min(float(v.lower()) for v in values);hi=min(float(v.upper()) for v in values)
+    llo=max(float(v.lower()) for v in values);lhi=max(float(v.upper()) for v in values)
+    imin=min(range(len(values)),key=lambda i:float(values[i].mid()))
+    imax=max(range(len(values)),key=lambda i:float(values[i].mid()))
+    return dict(K_interval=[float(np.nextafter(-hi,-np.inf)),float(np.nextafter(-lo,np.inf))],
+                Lambda_interval=[float(np.nextafter(llo,-np.inf)),float(np.nextafter(lhi,np.inf))],
+                K_ball=str(-values[imin]),Lambda_ball=str(values[imax]),arb_bits=ctx.prec)
+
+def tradeoffs():
+    known={}
+    for fn in ('e41_small.txt','e41_mid.txt'):
+        for line in (Path('examples/zp_half')/fn).read_text().splitlines():
+            mm=re.search(r'p=(\d+).*minM=([\d.]+).*P=([\d ]+)',line)
+            if mm:known[int(mm[1])]=(float(mm[2]),[int(x) for x in mm[3].split()])
+    out=[]
+    for q in (17,37,61,89,101,109):
+        h=(q-1)//2;m=(q-1)//4
+        C=2*np.cos(2*np.pi*np.outer(np.arange(1,h+1),np.arange(1,h+1))/q)
+        if q in known:kmin,seed=known[q];kmin_status='E41 double-precision enumeration, quoted'
+        else:
+            model=gp.Model();model.Params.OutputFlag=0;model.Params.Threads=4;model.Params.TimeLimit=8
+            model.Params.Seed=1913
+            b=model.addMVar(h,vtype=GRB.BINARY);kk=model.addVar(lb=0)
+            model.addConstr(b.sum()==m);model.addConstr(C@b+kk>=0)
+            model.setObjective(kk);model.optimize()
+            seed=(np.flatnonzero(b.X>.5)+1).tolist();kmin=float(kk.X)
+            kmin_status=f'Gurobi status {model.Status}, bound {model.ObjBound}'
+        seedarr=np.zeros(q);seedarr[seed]=1;seedarr[[-x for x in seed]]=1
+        F=np.fft.fft(seedarr).real;g=int(np.argmax(F[1:])+1)
+        seed=sorted(set(min((g*a)%q,q-(g*a)%q) for a in seed))
+        kbase=balls(q,seed)['K_interval'][1]
+        for factor in (1,1.025,1.075,1.15,1.35,1.7):
+            kap=kbase*factor+2e-8
+            model=gp.Model();model.Params.OutputFlag=0;model.Params.Threads=4
+            model.Params.TimeLimit=5 if q<=61 else 8
+            model.Params.MIPGap=0;model.Params.FeasibilityTol=1e-9;model.Params.IntFeasTol=1e-9
+            model.Params.Seed=1913
+            b=model.addMVar(h,vtype=GRB.BINARY,name='pair')
+            b.Start=np.isin(np.arange(1,h+1),seed).astype(float)
+            model.addConstr(b.sum()==m);model.addConstr(C@b>=-kap)
+            model.setObjective(C[0]@b,GRB.MAXIMIZE);model.optimize()
+            row=dict(q=q,kappa=kap,factor=factor,K_min_input=kbase,K_min_status=kmin_status,
+                     status=int(model.Status),runtime=model.Runtime,bound=model.ObjBound,
+                     solver=gp.gurobi.version(),solutions=model.SolCount)
+            if model.SolCount:
+                pairs=(np.flatnonzero(b.X>.5)+1).tolist()
+                row.update(pairs=pairs,objective=model.ObjVal,certificate=balls(q,pairs))
+            out.append(row)
+            (ROOT/'cyclic_tradeoffs.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,indent=2))
+            print(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in row.items() if k!='pairs'}),flush=True)
+    return out
+
+def profiles():
+    rows=[]
+    for q in (257,1021,4093,16381,65537):
+        rng=np.random.default_rng(1913000+q);h=(q-1)//2;m=(q-1)//4
+        a=np.arange(1,h+1);p=.5+.2*np.cos(2*np.pi*a/q)
+        bits=rng.random(h)<p
+        if bits.sum()>m:bits[rng.choice(np.flatnonzero(bits),int(bits.sum()-m),replace=False)]=False
+        elif bits.sum()<m:bits[rng.choice(np.flatnonzero(~bits),int(m-bits.sum()),replace=False)]=True
+        pairs=(np.flatnonzero(bits)+1).tolist();b=np.zeros(q);b[pairs]=1;b[[-a for a in pairs]]=1
+        F=np.fft.fft(b).real
+        row=dict(q=q,epsilon=.2,seed=1913000+q,n=int(b.sum()),K=float(-F[1:].min()),
+                 Lambda=float(F[1:].max()),lambda1=float(F[1]),pairs=pairs)
+        if q<=1021:row['certificate']=balls(q,pairs)
+        rows.append(row)
+        (ROOT/'cyclic_profiles.json').write_text(json.dumps(rows,indent=2))
+        print('PROFILE',json.dumps({k:v for k,v in row.items() if k!='pairs'}),flush=True)
+    return rows
+
+if __name__=='__main__':
+    print(platform.python_version(),np.__version__,gp.gurobi.version(),flush=True)
+    profiles();tradeoffs()
diff --git a/.research/agents/tdense13_scratch/diffuse.c b/.research/agents/tdense13_scratch/diffuse.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..db1054c8e545acfd280b8f692758f46d9c9949d2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.research/agents/tdense13_scratch/diffuse.c
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+#include <math.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+/* Profile-count-preserving sequential negative-error diffusion, 64 tracked modes. */
+void diffuse(int X,int F,int B,const double *p,const double *w,const double *angles,unsigned char *bits){
+ double *c=calloc(F,sizeof(double)),*s=calloc(F,sizeof(double));
+ double *ca=calloc(F,sizeof(double)),*sa=calloc(F,sizeof(double)),*v=calloc(F,sizeof(double));
+ for(int j=0;j<F;j++){c[j]=1;ca[j]=cos(angles[j]);sa[j]=sin(angles[j]);}
+ double carry=0;
+ for(int lo=0;lo<X;lo+=B){
+  int hi=lo+B;if(hi>X)hi=X;double target=carry;
+  for(int k=lo;k<hi;k++)target+=p[k];int need=(int)floor(target+.5);carry=target-need;
+  for(int k=lo;k<hi;k++){
+   double score[2]={0,0};
+   for(int j=0;j<F;j++){
+    double nc=c[j]*ca[j]-s[j]*sa[j];s[j]=s[j]*ca[j]+c[j]*sa[j];c[j]=nc;
+    for(int b=0;b<2;b++){double z=v[j]+(b-p[k])*w[k]*nc;if(z<0)score[b]+=z*z;}
+   }
+   int bit=score[1]<score[0];if(need==0)bit=0;if(need==hi-k)bit=1;
+   bits[k]=bit;need-=bit;
+   for(int j=0;j<F;j++)v[j]+=(bit-p[k])*w[k]*c[j];
+  }
+ }
+ free(c);free(s);free(ca);free(sa);free(v);
+}

