+HEURISTIC kill decision, limited to these implementations: all sampled size sequences have R>0.6 and increasing R. Stop these fixed-block laws rather than scaling them further. The q=o(X) texture dips occur close to cyclic roots and reflect the amplified local negative spectrum. The θ=1 interval and diffusion families instead show a fixed-block comb artifact: minimizing a finite collection of running spectral errors does not control untracked modes. The audit is measuring those rational modes and separating the smooth profile from the residual at each dip. These observations do not exclude optimized near-interval tails or all forms of spectral error diffusion.
